-- Migration version 21 -> 22: re-classify CruxCoach-authored climbs that were
-- imported from the Blossom blob as origin='kilter'.
--
-- The published blob can carry a CruxCoach-authored climb with origin='kilter'
-- (the blob's origin column is COALESCE(origin,'kilter') over the cron's work
-- DB and can lag the cruxcoach classification) while still carrying its setter
-- pubkey in created_by_pubkey. On a fresh install the blob is the only source,
-- so these climbs imported as origin='kilter' and stopped being recognised as
-- CruxCoach climbs — no edit/publish actions, missing from the cruxcoach
-- filter, no setter link.
--
-- A native Kilter climb never carries a created_by_pubkey, so that column is an
-- authoritative cruxcoach signal. The importer now derives origin from it on
-- insert; this heals the rows already on disk. Scoped to origin='kilter' rows
-- WITH a pubkey, so the Kilter catalogue (no pubkey) is untouched and any row
-- already correctly 'cruxcoach' is left as-is.
UPDATE climbs SET origin = 'cruxcoach'
WHERE origin = 'kilter'
  AND created_by_pubkey IS NOT NULL
  AND created_by_pubkey != '';
